I have everything needed. Here is my report.

## Summary

This is the **spring-petclinic-rest** app (Spring Boot 4.1.0, Java, Maven). All the "owner creation" business rules are implemented as small, self-contained AOP aspects / advices under `.../rest/advice/`, each hooked onto `ClinicService.saveOwner(..)`. The audit line is emitted by **one** such aspect (`OwnerAuditCreationAdvice`) via an SLF4J logger literally named `"AUDIT"`. There is currently **no `AuditEvent` class and no structured event emission** — only a single free-text log line. A `memberId` field does **not** exist anywhere in production code; it appears only in a test comment describing a future direction.

---

## 1. Owner creation flow

**Controller (the single create endpoint `POST /api/owners`):**
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`

```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```

**Service:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java` (lines 232-237) — the join point every owner aspect targets:

```java
@Override
@Transactional
public void saveOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}
```

Interface: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicService.java` (line 59, `void saveOwner(Owner owner)`).

The many `Owner*Advice` classes in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/` each implement one owner-creation rule (customer code, namesake count, household size, membership cap, daily creation limit, duplicate detection, audit, etc.).

---

## 2. The existing audit-emitting code (the "audit line")

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/OwnerAuditCreationAdvice.java` — this is the exact code that logs on owner creation:

```java
@Aspect
@Component
public class OwnerAuditCreationAdvice {

